{"at": "2026-11-25T09:46:37.024Z", "run": "20261125-0137-verify-debrid-5636", "unit": "u20", "op": "set", "rid": "debrid/offcloud-lifetime-via-stacksocial", "path": "$.reliability_note", "old": "Buyers report the lifetime was replaced: 'I purchased this service during their last Lifetime StackSocial sale in October 2025. Today in January 2026, they claim that a member of staff passed and they are changing everything' (2026-01-24); 'given a 1 year free premium. Now my account instead of being a lifetime premium' (2026-02-18). A Taiwanese buyer got the same answer from support on 2026-01-21: the old lifetime is invalid and the compensation is one year. Trustpilot's aggregate was 1.7/5 from 86 reviews on 2026-11-03.", "new": "Buyers report the lifetime was replaced: a review dated 2026-10-21 states 'I bought lifetime plan but they converted it to one year premium.' and a review dated 2026-11-06 states 'Company offered a lifetime service and now refuses to honor it.' A Taiwanese buyer got the same answer from support on 2026-01-21: the old lifetime is invalid and the compensation is one year. Trustpilot's aggregate is 1.7 from 87 reviews on 2026-11-25. The vendor's home page states a new team took over and rebuilt the service, and offers only monthly and yearly plans, with no refund policy.", "rung": "reported", "evidence": {"url": "https://www.trustpilot.com/reviews/6ad90e39c2097c694aa8c201", "date": "2026-11-25", "proved": "a Trustpilot review dated 2026-10-21 reports a lifetime plan converted to one year", "capture": "sha256:34897e6d11ceb8a6a37227918d83d5ec867f16fa094ec31970f7e28a515ede58", "quote": "I bought lifetime plan but they converted it to one year premium."}, "added": true, "reason": "new dated reviews and the vendor's rebuilt-service statement replace the older reliability summary"}
